# Chapter 4 — Ansible Vault + HashiCorp Vault + KMS Auto-Unseal

## Ansible Vault — Bootstrap Phase Encryption

Before HashiCorp Vault exists, I still need to pass secrets to playbooks without committing them to Git.
Ansible Vault is just an encryption tool — not a secret store. I encrypt sensitive values using
`ansible-vault encrypt_string` and the resulting `!vault` blocks go into group_vars files. The password
to decrypt them lives in AWS Secrets Manager at `{env}/ansible/vault-password`.

At runtime: workflow fetches the vault password from Secrets Manager → writes it to `~/.ansible_vault`
on the ansible node → `ansible.cfg` points to that file path → when Ansible loads group_vars it
decrypts the `!vault` blocks automatically.

