## Where Is the "Vault Master Key"

Never explicitly configured — it was generated automatically during `vault operator init`:

```
vault operator init ran
  → Vault generated a master key (random, never shown to anyone)
  → Vault saw seal "awskms" { kms_key_id = "alias/vault-unseal" } in vault.hcl
  → Vault sent master key to KMS → KMS encrypted it → returned ciphertext
  → Vault stored the ciphertext inside /opt/vault/data (Raft storage)
  → Vault generated 5 recovery keys from the master key → saved to Secrets Manager
```

The encrypted master key lives embedded inside Vault's Raft storage. Not a visible file. Every restart:
Vault reads that encrypted blob → sends to KMS → gets decrypted → unsealed.

